    {
     "identifier": "KS-1903",
     "title": "check-dockerfile-non-root.sh: a final USER of root:root, 0:0 or ROOT passes the non-root guard with OK",
     "state": {
      "name": "Backlog"
     },
     "description": "**BLUF:** `Blockchain/Dev/scripts/check-dockerfile-non-root.sh` prints `OK` for a Dockerfile whose final `USER` is `root:root`, `0:0` or `ROOT`, because it compares the last `USER` value to `root` and `0` exactly. Pre-existing; pull request 1851 (KS-1866) corrects other faults in the same script and does not touch this comparison.\n\n* **Cause** (read at the pull request 1851 head `1c73d6ea5d39`): `check-dockerfile-non-root.sh:27` strips whitespace from the last `USER` value and `:32` tests `= \"root\"` or `= \"0\"` only.\n* **Measured here** with the real script copied into a private fixture tree, one Dockerfile per case, run from the tree: `USER root` rc 1 reported (control); `USER 0` rc 1 reported (control); `USER app` rc 0 `OK` (control); `USER root:root` rc 0 `OK \u2014 all 1 Dockerfile(s) drop root for runtime.`; `USER 0:0` rc 0 `OK`; `USER ROOT` rc 0 `OK`.\n* **Searched the board** for `check-dockerfile-non-root`, `USER root:root`: the hits were KS-1866 (the pull request's own ticket), KS-937 and KS-930 (a different guard, the re-link guard) and KS-1080 (a container that runs as root, not this guard); none covers the comparison.\n* **Not measured:** the real Dockerfiles in the tree (none was checked for these spellings); GNU/Linux behaviour. Fix shape not chosen here (for example strip a `:group` suffix and compare case-insensitively, and treat `0` and `root` after that).\n* **Discovered:** 2026-10-31, Seat R 68th, during merge prep of pull request 1851 (gate 50 finding F-851-2); filed on Wednesday's word.",
     "comments": {
      "nodes": []
     }
    }
   ]
  }
 }
}
