 "data": {
  "issues": {
   "nodes": [
    {
     "identifier": "KS-1884",
     "title": "manifest_readers_agree.test.sh drivers discard stderr, so a tool failure reads as a reader disagreement and its reason is lost (cause unmeasured)",
     "state": {
      "name": "Backlog"
     },
     "description": "## BLUF\n\n`systemTest/__tests__/manifest_readers_agree.test.sh` **throws away the reason a driver failed, so one tool failure reads as a reader disagreement.** On 2026-10-30 this failed a 30-minute pre-push hook once. **The cause is unmeasured**, because the error text was discarded.\n\nFacts only. No code was touched.\n\n## What happened\n\nKS-1384 F0a's push, head `969df4571d45`, 08:15:47Z to 08:45:18Z (1,771 s), was refused at preflight leg 14:\n\n`FAIL '   ' -> unslotted \u2014 expected all four = 'actors-unslotted.json'; writer='' playwright='actors-unslotted.json' performance='actors-unslotted.json' schemathesis='actors-unslotted.json'`\n\n23 passed, 1 failed. The writer driver answered nothing for that one case. The same driver answered correctly for the other 23 cases in the same run. The push lost its place in the queue.\n\n## Why it is in the test, not the change\n\n* Where: the `writer`, `playwright`, `performance` and `schemathesis` driver functions each end `2>/dev/null | tail -1`. Anything that stops a driver printing, such as a tool start-up failure, leaves an empty string, and `case_` then reports a disagreement between readers. The harness cannot tell \"this reader names another file\" from \"this reader did not run\".\n* F0a changes no path under `systemTest`.\n* KS-1384 F-a's push, an hour earlier, passed this test 24 of 24.\n* Alone, in F0a's own worktree at the same head: 3 of 3 runs, each 24 of 24 (32 to 37 s each, load average up to 13).\n* No other seat's saved `push.out` from October shows this test failing.\n\n## Cause: unmeasured\n\nTwo candidates were read and neither is supported:\n\n* KS-1135's long `TMPDIR`: this host's `TMPDIR` is 48 characters, nowhere near the \\~104-byte limit.\n* A stale tsx socket: 0 sockets in the tsx temp directory after the failure (read a few minutes later, so this does not exclude one that existed during the run).\n\nThis is not stated as a flake. One failure in the runs measured says only that it is rare here.\n\n## What is open\n\nKeeping the driver's stderr when it prints nothing would let the next failure name its cause. A driver that answered empty could also be reported as \"did not run\", apart from a real disagreement. Nothing is proposed beyond that. Other shell suites may share the pattern; that is not measured.\n\n## Searched before filing (title, description and comments, archived included; controls: a literal in archived KS-336 found, a nonsense token 0)\n\n* `manifest_readers_agree` 7. Read the nearest: **KS-1138** is this test red on ubuntu with the schemathesis reader answering ERROR, a different defect; **KS-1135** is the long-TMPDIR failure, Done; KS-877, KS-971, KS-1075, KS-1078 and KS-1148 name the test in passing.\n* `discard stderr`, `discards stderr`, `2>/dev/null | tail -1`: 0 each.\n\nRefs KS-1384, KS-1138.",
     "comments": {
      "nodes": []
     }
    }
   ]
  }
 }
}
